-- Tests for pc-general.l4 - Chapter 2 of the Penal Code 1871 (ss 6-52B), the
-- Punishment record (ss 41, 53) and the form of a charge (CPC 2010 ss 123-126).
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: each Illustration Chapter 2 prints is
-- cited as `-- s N illus (x)`; boundary cases for s 40 and s 41 are cited to
-- the words they test. A failing assertion here is a finding, not a typo.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Chapter 2 - tests`

§§ `s 10`

#ASSERT `man within section 10` male
#ASSERT NOT `man within section 10` female
#ASSERT `woman within section 10` female

§§ `s 19 - judge`

`no judicial power` MEANS `Judge Facts` WITH
    `officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if not appealed against, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if confirmed by some other authority, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS FALSE

-- s 19 illus (a): a Magistrate with power to sentence to fine or imprisonment,
-- WITH appeal (a judgment definitive if not appealed against) is a judge ...
`a Magistrate with power to sentence, subject to appeal` MEANS `Judge Facts` WITH
    `officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if not appealed against, would be definitive` IS TRUE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if confirmed by some other authority, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `judge within section 19` `a Magistrate with power to sentence, subject to appeal`

-- ... and WITHOUT appeal (a definitive judgment).
`a Magistrate with power to sentence, without appeal` MEANS `Judge Facts` WITH
    `officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS TRUE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if not appealed against, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if confirmed by some other authority, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `judge within section 19` `a Magistrate with power to sentence, without appeal`

-- s 19 illus (b): officers holding an inquiry into the loss of a ship under the
-- Merchant Shipping Act 1995 are judges - as a body empowered to give such a
-- judgment.
`officers holding a ship-loss inquiry` MEANS `Judge Facts` WITH
    `officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if not appealed against, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `empowered by law to give a judgment which, if confirmed by some other authority, would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `judge within section 19` `officers holding a ship-loss inquiry`

-- s 19 illus (c): a Magistrate with power only to commit for trial is not a judge.
#ASSERT NOT `judge within section 19` `no judicial power`

§§ `s 20 - court of justice`

#ASSERT `court of justice within section 20` (`Court Facts` WITH `a judge empowered by law to act judicially alone` IS TRUE, `a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body` IS FALSE, `acting judicially` IS TRUE)
-- "when such judge or body of judges is acting judicially" - not otherwise
#ASSERT NOT `court of justice within section 20` (`Court Facts` WITH `a judge empowered by law to act judicially alone` IS TRUE, `a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body` IS FALSE, `acting judicially` IS FALSE)

§§ `s 21 - public servant`

`no public office` MEANS Office WITH
    description IS "a private individual"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS FALSE
    `is a judge` IS FALSE
    `officer of a court of justice with a judicial duty` IS FALSE
    `assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant` IS FALSE
    `arbitrator or referee of a court or competent public authority` IS FALSE
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement` IS FALSE
    `officer of the Government or of a statutory body for a public function` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining law and order` IS FALSE
    `duty of preserving the public peace` IS FALSE
    `duty of preventing and detecting offences` IS FALSE
    `duty of apprehending offenders or bringing them to justice` IS FALSE
    `duty of executing legal processes` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining order in the premises of the courts` IS FALSE
    `duty of escorting and guarding prisoners and accused persons in remand` IS FALSE
    `duty of protecting public health or safety or preventing public inconvenience` IS FALSE
    `officer with a duty touching the property or pecuniary interests of Government, or in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated for a public duty` IS FALSE
    `member of the Public Service, Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission` IS FALSE
    `employed to carry out a duty in paragraph (g)(i) to (vii) on behalf of the Government or a statutory body` IS FALSE
    `performing such duties at the time` IS FALSE
    `a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS FALSE

-- s 21(1)(g)(iii): an officer of the Government whose duty is preventing and
-- detecting offences - a police officer (s 6 illus (b) calls one "A, a police
-- officer").
`a police officer` MEANS Office WITH
    description IS "a police officer"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS FALSE
    `is a judge` IS FALSE
    `officer of a court of justice with a judicial duty` IS FALSE
    `assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant` IS FALSE
    `arbitrator or referee of a court or competent public authority` IS FALSE
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement` IS FALSE
    `officer of the Government or of a statutory body for a public function` IS TRUE
    `duty of maintaining law and order` IS FALSE
    `duty of preserving the public peace` IS FALSE
    `duty of preventing and detecting offences` IS TRUE
    `duty of apprehending offenders or bringing them to justice` IS FALSE
    `duty of executing legal processes` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining order in the premises of the courts` IS FALSE
    `duty of escorting and guarding prisoners and accused persons in remand` IS FALSE
    `duty of protecting public health or safety or preventing public inconvenience` IS FALSE
    `officer with a duty touching the property or pecuniary interests of Government, or in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated for a public duty` IS FALSE
    `member of the Public Service, Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission` IS FALSE
    `employed to carry out a duty in paragraph (g)(i) to (vii) on behalf of the Government or a statutory body` IS FALSE
    `performing such duties at the time` IS FALSE
    `a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `public servant within section 21` `a police officer`
#ASSERT NOT `public servant within section 21` `no public office`

-- s 21(1)(g) needs BOTH the office and one of the duties in (i)-(viii): a
-- Government officer with none of them is not a public servant under (g).
`a Government officer with no (g) duty` MEANS Office WITH
    description IS "a Government officer"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS FALSE
    `is a judge` IS FALSE
    `officer of a court of justice with a judicial duty` IS FALSE
    `assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant` IS FALSE
    `arbitrator or referee of a court or competent public authority` IS FALSE
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement` IS FALSE
    `officer of the Government or of a statutory body for a public function` IS TRUE
    `duty of maintaining law and order` IS FALSE
    `duty of preserving the public peace` IS FALSE
    `duty of preventing and detecting offences` IS FALSE
    `duty of apprehending offenders or bringing them to justice` IS FALSE
    `duty of executing legal processes` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining order in the premises of the courts` IS FALSE
    `duty of escorting and guarding prisoners and accused persons in remand` IS FALSE
    `duty of protecting public health or safety or preventing public inconvenience` IS FALSE
    `officer with a duty touching the property or pecuniary interests of Government, or in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated for a public duty` IS FALSE
    `member of the Public Service, Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission` IS FALSE
    `employed to carry out a duty in paragraph (g)(i) to (vii) on behalf of the Government or a statutory body` IS FALSE
    `performing such duties at the time` IS FALSE
    `a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `public servant within section 21` `a Government officer with no (g) duty`

-- s 21(1)(j): a contractor employed to escort prisoners is a public servant only
-- "when that person is performing such duties".
`an escort contractor, on duty` MEANS Office WITH
    description IS "a contracted prisoner escort"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS FALSE
