    `duty of preserving the public peace` IS FALSE
    `duty of preventing and detecting offences` IS FALSE
    `duty of apprehending offenders or bringing them to justice` IS FALSE
    `duty of executing legal processes` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining order in the premises of the courts` IS FALSE
    `duty of escorting and guarding prisoners and accused persons in remand` IS FALSE
    `duty of protecting public health or safety or preventing public inconvenience` IS FALSE
    `officer with a duty touching the property or pecuniary interests of Government, or in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated for a public duty` IS FALSE
    `member of the Public Service, Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission` IS FALSE
    `employed to carry out a duty in paragraph (g)(i) to (vii) on behalf of the Government or a statutory body` IS TRUE
    `performing such duties at the time` IS FALSE
    `a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `public servant within section 21` `an escort contractor, on duty`
#ASSERT NOT `public servant within section 21` `an escort contractor, off duty`

-- s 21(2): a judge within the AJPA is a public servant, but not for ss 175,
-- 178, 179, 180 and 228.
`an AJPA judge` MEANS Office WITH
    description IS "a Judge of the Supreme Court"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS FALSE
    `is a judge` IS TRUE
    `officer of a court of justice with a judicial duty` IS FALSE
    `assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant` IS FALSE
    `arbitrator or referee of a court or competent public authority` IS FALSE
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement` IS FALSE
    `officer of the Government or of a statutory body for a public function` IS FALSE
    `duty of maintaining law and order` IS FALSE
