#ASSERT `public servant within section 21, for sections 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228` `a police officer`

§§ `s 22 - property`

-- s 22 illus: "Writings, relating to real or personal property or rights, are
-- movable property." A title deed is not land, nor fastened to it.
`a title deed` MEANS `Property` WITH
    description IS "the title deed to a house"
    `is land` IS FALSE
    `is a benefit to arise out of land` IS FALSE
    `is a thing attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS FALSE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money's worth` IS FALSE
    `can be digitally traded` IS FALSE
    `functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or store of value` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `movable property within section 22` `a title deed`
#ASSERT NOT `immovable property within section 22` `a title deed`

-- "things ... permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth"
`a door fastened to a house` MEANS `Property` WITH
    description IS "a door fastened to a house"
    `is land` IS FALSE
    `is a benefit to arise out of land` IS FALSE
    `is a thing attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS TRUE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS FALSE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money's worth` IS FALSE
    `can be digitally traded` IS FALSE
    `functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or store of value` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `immovable property within section 22` `a door fastened to a house`
#ASSERT NOT `movable property within section 22` `a door fastened to a house`

-- "virtual currency": all three limbs, "regardless of whether it is legal tender"
`a digital token` MEANS `Property` WITH
    description IS "0.5 units of a cryptocurrency"
    `is land` IS FALSE
    `is a benefit to arise out of land` IS FALSE
    `is a thing attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS TRUE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money's worth` IS TRUE
    `can be digitally traded` IS TRUE
    `functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or store of value` IS TRUE
`a digital token that cannot be traded` MEANS `Property` WITH
    description IS "a non-transferable loyalty point"
    `is land` IS FALSE
    `is a benefit to arise out of land` IS FALSE
    `is a thing attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS TRUE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money's worth` IS TRUE
    `can be digitally traded` IS FALSE
    `functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or store of value` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `virtual currency within section 22` `a digital token`
#ASSERT NOT `virtual currency within section 22` `a digital token that cannot be traded`
-- and virtual currency is movable property (property of every description, except immovable)
#ASSERT `movable property within section 22` `a digital token`

§§ `ss 23-25 - wrongful gain and loss, dishonestly, fraudulently`

#ASSERT `wrongful gain within section 23` (`Gain or Loss Facts` WITH `gain by unlawful means of property to which the person gaining it is not legally entitled` IS FALSE, `avoidance by unlawful means of a loss of property which the person is not legally entitled to avoid` IS TRUE, `loss by unlawful means of property to which the person losing it is legally entitled` IS FALSE, `exposure of risk to a loss by unlawful means of property to which the person exposed is legally entitled` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `wrongful loss within section 23` (`Gain or Loss Facts` WITH `gain by unlawful means of property to which the person gaining it is not legally entitled` IS FALSE, `avoidance by unlawful means of a loss of property which the person is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE, `loss by unlawful means of property to which the person losing it is legally entitled` IS FALSE, `exposure of risk to a loss by unlawful means of property to which the person exposed is legally entitled` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `wrongful loss within section 23` (`Gain or Loss Facts` WITH `gain by unlawful means of property to which the person gaining it is not legally entitled` IS TRUE, `avoidance by unlawful means of a loss of property which the person is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE, `loss by unlawful means of property to which the person losing it is legally entitled` IS FALSE, `exposure of risk to a loss by unlawful means of property to which the person exposed is legally entitled` IS FALSE)

-- s 24 (a) alone suffices; (b) needs both the standard and the knowledge
#ASSERT `dishonestly within section 24` (`Dishonesty Facts` WITH `intention of causing wrongful gain to A or another person` IS TRUE, `intention of causing wrongful loss to another person` IS FALSE, `dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE, `A knows that that act is dishonest by such standards` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `dishonestly within section 24` (`Dishonesty Facts` WITH `intention of causing wrongful gain to A or another person` IS FALSE, `intention of causing wrongful loss to another person` IS FALSE, `dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE, `A knows that that act is dishonest by such standards` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `dishonestly within section 24` (`Dishonesty Facts` WITH `intention of causing wrongful gain to A or another person` IS FALSE, `intention of causing wrongful loss to another person` IS FALSE, `dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE, `A knows that that act is dishonest by such standards` IS FALSE)

-- s 25; Explanation 1 defeats a trifle
#ASSERT `fraudulently within section 25` (`Fraud Facts` WITH `intent to deceive another person` IS TRUE, `an advantage should accrue to A or another person` IS TRUE, `detriment should befall B or another person other than A` IS FALSE, `the advantage or detriment intended is so slight that no reasonable person would complain of it` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `fraudulently within section 25` (`Fraud Facts` WITH `intent to deceive another person` IS TRUE, `an advantage should accrue to A or another person` IS TRUE, `detriment should befall B or another person other than A` IS FALSE, `the advantage or detriment intended is so slight that no reasonable person would complain of it` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `fraudulently within section 25` (`Fraud Facts` WITH `intent to deceive another person` IS FALSE, `an advantage should accrue to A or another person` IS TRUE, `detriment should befall B or another person other than A` IS TRUE, `the advantage or detriment intended is so slight that no reasonable person would complain of it` IS FALSE)

§§ `ss 26-26B`

#ASSERT `reason to believe within section 26` (`Belief Facts` WITH `sufficient cause to believe that thing` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reason to believe within section 26` (`Belief Facts` WITH `sufficient cause to believe that thing` IS FALSE)

-- s 26A illus: A sets fire to an inhabited house by night to facilitate a
-- robbery and causes a death. He may not have intended death; "yet, if he knew
-- that he was likely to cause death, he has caused death voluntarily."
#ASSERT `voluntarily within section 26A` (`Voluntariness Facts` WITH `caused it by means whereby he intended to cause it` IS FALSE, `knew the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS TRUE, `had reason to believe the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS FALSE)
-- and "reason to believe" the means likely suffices too
#ASSERT `voluntarily within section 26A` (`Voluntariness Facts` WITH `caused it by means whereby he intended to cause it` IS FALSE, `knew the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS FALSE, `had reason to believe the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `voluntarily within section 26A` (`Voluntariness Facts` WITH `caused it by means whereby he intended to cause it` IS FALSE, `knew the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS FALSE, `had reason to believe the means to be likely to cause it when employing them` IS FALSE)

-- s 26B: without due care and attention, nothing is in good faith
#ASSERT NOT `in good faith within section 26B` (`Good Faith Facts` WITH `done or believed with due care and attention` IS FALSE)

§§ `ss 26C-26F - the fault words`

`a clear mind` MEANS `Fault Facts` WITH
    `did the act deliberately` IS FALSE
    `with the purpose of causing that effect` IS FALSE
    `knowing that that effect would be virtually certain to result` IS FALSE
    `aware that the circumstance exists, will exist or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `aware that the effect will be caused or is virtually certain to be caused` IS FALSE
    `knowing that there is a real risk that the circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE
    `knowing that there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS FALSE
    `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE
    `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE
    `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE

-- s 26C(2)(b): virtual certainty is intention, without purpose
#ASSERT `causes the effect intentionally within section 26C(2)` (`Fault Facts` WITH `did the act deliberately` IS TRUE, `with the purpose of causing that effect` IS FALSE, `knowing that that effect would be virtually certain to result` IS TRUE, `aware that the circumstance exists, will exist or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE, `aware that the effect will be caused or is virtually certain to be caused` IS TRUE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS TRUE, `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS TRUE, `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE, `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `causes the effect intentionally within section 26C(2)` `a clear mind`
#ASSERT NOT `negligently within section 26F` `a clear mind`

-- s 26E: a real risk it was REASONABLE to take is not rashness
#ASSERT NOT `rashly in respect of an effect within section 26E(2)` (`Fault Facts` WITH `did the act deliberately` IS TRUE, `with the purpose of causing that effect` IS FALSE, `knowing that that effect would be virtually certain to result` IS FALSE, `aware that the circumstance exists, will exist or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE, `aware that the effect will be caused or is virtually certain to be caused` IS FALSE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS TRUE, `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE, `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE, `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `rashly in respect of an effect within section 26E(2)` (`Fault Facts` WITH `did the act deliberately` IS TRUE, `with the purpose of causing that effect` IS FALSE, `knowing that that effect would be virtually certain to result` IS FALSE, `aware that the circumstance exists, will exist or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE, `aware that the effect will be caused or is virtually certain to be caused` IS FALSE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE, `knowing that there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS TRUE, `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS TRUE, `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE, `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE)

-- s 26D(3): knowingly is established by intention or wilful blindness
#ASSERT `the fault element` knowingly `is established by` intentionally
#ASSERT `the fault element` knowingly `is established by` `with wilful blindness`
#ASSERT NOT (`the fault element` knowingly `is established by` rashly)
-- s 26E(3): rashly is established by intention or knowledge
#ASSERT `the fault element` rashly `is established by` knowingly
#ASSERT NOT (`the fault element` rashly `is established by` negligently)
-- s 26F(2): negligently is established by intention, knowledge or rashness
#ASSERT `the fault element` negligently `is established by` rashly
#ASSERT `the fault element` negligently `is established by` intentionally
-- nothing lower establishes intention
#ASSERT NOT (`the fault element` intentionally `is established by` knowingly)
-- FORK G-4: s 26E(3) does not list wilful blindness, and the literal reading
-- does not chain it through s 26D(3)
#ASSERT NOT (`the fault element` rashly `is established by` `with wilful blindness`)

§§ `s 26G - transferred fault`

-- s 26G(3) illus (a): A throws a stone at B intending to hurt B; it hurts C. A
-- commits voluntarily causing hurt in respect of C if he threw it negligently
-- in respect of C.
`the stone that hurt C` MEANS `Transferred Fault Facts` WITH
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS TRUE
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS FALSE
    `all the fault elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `all the physical elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception applies` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements included an act or effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused believed or intended that it would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `done negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS TRUE
-- s 26G(3) illus (b), the stone aimed at B's vase that damages C's clay pot
-- (mischief in respect of C), has the same shape on these atoms.
#ASSERT `guilty despite transferred fault within section 26G` `the stone that hurt C`

-- s 26G(3) illus (c): "B, I will kill you", heard by C. A threatened no injury
-- to C, so the physical elements of criminal intimidation against C are not
-- proven, and s 26G does not supply them.
`the threat C overheard` MEANS `Transferred Fault Facts` WITH
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS TRUE
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS FALSE
    `all the fault elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `all the physical elements of the offence are proven` IS FALSE
    `a defence or exception applies` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements included an act or effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused believed or intended that it would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `done negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `guilty despite transferred fault within section 26G` `the threat C overheard`

-- s 26G(4) illus (a), (b) and (c): the stone that hits a vase (mischief), a
-- police officer (s 332) or causes grievous hurt (s 325) - in each A lacked the
-- FAULT element of the graver offence, and s 26G(4) keeps it required.
`the stone, without the fault element` MEANS `Transferred Fault Facts` WITH
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS TRUE
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS FALSE
    `all the fault elements of the offence are proven` IS FALSE
    `all the physical elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception applies` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements included an act or effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused believed or intended that it would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `done negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `guilty despite transferred fault within section 26G` `the stone, without the fault element`

-- s 26G(5) illus: A throws the stone at B in private defence and hurts C; A
-- may rely on private defence against B. With the defence applying, no guilt.
`the stone thrown in private defence` MEANS `Transferred Fault Facts` WITH
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS TRUE
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS FALSE
    `all the fault elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `all the physical elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception applies` IS TRUE
    `the physical elements included an act or effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused believed or intended that it would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `done negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `guilty despite transferred fault within section 26G` `the stone thrown in private defence`

-- s 26G(1): "except where section 301(1) applies"
`a death by transferred malice` MEANS `Transferred Fault Facts` WITH
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS TRUE
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS TRUE
    `all the fault elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `all the physical elements of the offence are proven` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception applies` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements included an act or effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused believed or intended that it would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `done negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `guilty despite transferred fault within section 26G` `a death by transferred malice`

